{#- Reply to a police / LEA hold request (wapsi.verify.lea_request): the hold is limited to the disputed amount the
    bank can identify on the money trail, and missing checklist fields are asked for. Numbers come from the request
    and the case data (`c`); typed-in text is neutralised before it reaches this template. -#}
# Reply to hold request {{ c.request_id }}{{ c.title_suffix }}

- **To:** {{ c.to_line }}
- **From:** Nodal Officer (Cyber Fraud Cell), {{ c.bank_name }}
- **Your reference:** {{ c.ref_line }}

## Hold

{% if c.has_identifiable %}
The bank will hold {{ c.identifiable }} in A/c No. {{ c.account_id }}, subject to the nodal officer's approval: the disputed amount it can identify on the money trail ({{ c.basis }}) [SOP-9-1] [SOP-ANNEX-I].
{% else %}
No amount can be held on this request yet: the bank cannot identify the disputed amount from the details received ({{ c.basis }}) [SOP-9-1].
{% endif %}
{% if c.over_requested %}

The request asks for {{ c.requested }}; only the identifiable amount above is held, because the rest cannot be tied to victim money still in the account.
{% endif %}
{% if c.asks_account_level %}

The request asks for action on the whole account. Holds are amount-specific by default, and unwarranted orders freezing accounts are discouraged [SOP-5-IX]. Account-level action is taken only as a recorded exception approved by a supervisor; please state the specific amount, or send an order that specifies account-level action and its grounds.
{% endif %}
{% if c.matched_utrs %}

- Disputed credits identified on the trail: UTR/TRX ID {{ c.matched_utrs }}.
{% endif %}
{% if c.unmatched_utrs %}
- References not found as credits into the account on the trail: {{ c.unmatched_utrs }}.
{% endif %}

{% if c.complete %}
## Details

The request carries every detail the bank needs: complaint reference, requesting officer and rank, jurisdiction, account number, amount, transaction references, legal provision, and date and validity.
{% else %}
## Details needed

Please send the following so that the hold can be reviewed:

{% for m in c.missing %}
- {{ m.label }}: {{ m.problem }}.
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

The request is handled under the notice procedure of Section 168 read with Section 94 BNSS that the SOP sets out [BNSS-168] [BNSS-94].

Nodal Officer (Cyber Fraud Cell)
{{ c.bank_name }}
